@feat-rag-05 @provider-conditional-prompt @think-block-handling
Feature: Provider-conditional Player system prompt and <think>-block handling

  As an operator running the architect role across cloud and local providers
  I want the Player system prompt to switch automatically to the GOAL.md-trained
  prompt when AGENT_MODELS__REASONING_MODEL=local and to strip <think>...</think>
  blocks before Coach evaluation while preserving them in the session log
  So that the SLM-vs-frontier comparison thesis (FEAT-RAG-07-03) is fair —
  the fine-tune is run against the prompt it was trained on, the Coach is not
  scoring chain-of-thought, and full reasoning traces remain auditable.

  Background:
    Given the architect role is loaded from roles/architect/
    And the Phase 0 Player prompt exists at roles/architect/prompts/player.md
    And the GOAL.md-trained prompt is bundled with the architect role
    And the prompt loader exposes a resolve_player_prompt(provider) entry point

  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  # GROUP A: Key Examples
  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  # Why: Load-bearing thesis path — when running the local fine-tune, the
  #       prompt it was trained against must be loaded verbatim or the
  #       FEAT-RAG-07-03 comparison is not fair (per OD-2 resolution).
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] The trained prompt artefact lives at
  #       roles/architect/prompts/player_trained.md, snapshot of GOAL.md
  #       §System Prompt (ASSUM-001).
  @task:TASK-RAG05-001
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Local provider loads the GOAL.md-trained Player system prompt verbatim
    Given AGENT_MODELS__REASONING_MODEL is set to "local"
    When the orchestrator resolves the Player system prompt for the architect role
    Then the resolved prompt should be the GOAL.md-trained architect prompt verbatim
    And the resolved prompt should not be modified, wrapped, or augmented

  # Why: Cloud baseline runs (the GPT-5.5 FinProxy baseline used "claude" via
  #       the existing AGENT_MODELS path) must keep using the Phase 0 Player
  #       prompt — the comparison loses meaning if both sides shift.
  @task:TASK-RAG05-001
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario Outline: Cloud providers continue to use the Phase 0 Player prompt
    Given AGENT_MODELS__REASONING_MODEL is set to "<provider>"
    When the orchestrator resolves the Player system prompt for the architect role
    Then the resolved prompt should be the existing Phase 0 architect Player prompt
    And the resolved prompt should not be the GOAL.md-trained prompt

    Examples:
      | provider |
      | claude   |
      | gemini   |
      | openai   |

  # Why: The fine-tune emits <think>...</think> followed by the answer; the
  #       Coach must score only the answer (per OD-3) so style criteria
  #       like trade-off acknowledgement are evaluated on the visible
  #       response, not the chain-of-thought.
  @task:TASK-RAG05-002
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: <think> blocks are stripped from Player output before Coach evaluation
    Given the Player produced output containing a <think>...</think> block followed by an answer
    When the orchestrator prepares the Player output for Coach evaluation
    Then the content sent to the Coach should not contain any <think>...</think> block
    And the visible answer should be preserved unchanged

  # Why: Traceability — operators reviewing a session need to see the
  #       fine-tune's reasoning to diagnose failures. Stripping for the
  #       Coach must not strip from the audit trail.
  @task:TASK-RAG05-002
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Full <think> reasoning is preserved in the session log
    Given the Player produced output containing a <think>...</think> block followed by an answer
    When the orchestrator records the Player output to the session log
    Then the session log entry should contain the full output including the <think> block
    And the session log entry should be marked as the raw Player output

