  # Why: Two-model split (Player=local, Coach=claude) is endorsed by
  #       phase-rag-build-plan §Risk Mitigation. Prompt selection must
  #       follow the *Player's* provider, not the Coach's, or the local
  #       Player will receive the cloud prompt.
  @task:TASK-RAG05-001
  @edge-case @regression
  Scenario: Two-model split — Player=local, Coach=claude — selects prompts per-role
    Given the Player provider is "local"
    And the Coach provider is "claude"
    When the orchestrator resolves prompts for both roles
    Then the Player prompt should be the GOAL.md-trained architect prompt
    And the Coach prompt should be the existing Phase 0 architect Coach prompt

  # Why: The stripping helper sits in the rejection-revision loop too —
  #       on retry, the Player's revised output (still containing
  #       <think>) must be stripped again before going to the Coach,
  #       not just on the first turn.
  @task:TASK-RAG05-002
  @edge-case
  Scenario: <think> stripping applies on revision turns, not just the first attempt
    Given the Coach rejected the Player's first output
    And the Player produced a revised output containing a <think>...</think> block
    When the orchestrator prepares the revised output for Coach evaluation
    Then the content sent to the Coach should not contain any <think>...</think> block
    And the session log should retain the full revised output for the revision turn

  # Why: D5 invariant — the new prompt-selection logic must not change
