  #       <think>...</think> tag pairs are treated as reasoning blocks
  #       (ASSUM-007).
  @task:TASK-RAG05-002
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Literal <think> text inside a fenced code block is preserved
    Given the Player produced output containing a fenced code block that mentions the literal string "<think>"
    When the orchestrator prepares the Player output for Coach evaluation
    Then the content sent to the Coach should still contain the fenced code block intact
    And the literal "<think>" inside the code block should not be stripped

